<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 1-wk T-bills 26 pct sold, yield 3.71 pct.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 1-wk T-bills 26 pct sold, yield 3.71 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry offer of five billion levs of one-week discount T-bills was 26 percent sold, yielding 3.71 percent until maturity, the Bulgarian National Bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		     BG 3010197005</p>
<p> Par value			  5.0 billion levs</p>
<p> Auction date		     January 6, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date			 January 8, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		    January 15, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		    5.0 bln levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids		96.02 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		    1.3 bln levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	     96.42 pct</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity    3.71 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
